WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[rock music playing]

00:43.043 --> 00:45.129
-Want to go have some tteokbokki?
-Yeah, sounds good.

00:45.212 --> 00:47.339
CHAPTER 12: YOU GUYS WANT TO GO
OUT INTO THE REAL WORLD, RIGHT?

00:47.423 --> 00:48.424
[sighs]

00:55.097 --> 00:56.891
Huh? Hello, Mr. Yoon.

00:56.974 --> 00:58.559
Eui-ju, you haven't gone home yet?

00:58.642 --> 01:02.062
Uh, no, I'm going to stop by
the library before I leave.

01:03.147 --> 01:04.315
Is something bothering you?

01:06.567 --> 01:07.860
[sighs]

01:07.943 --> 01:09.361
It's my homeroom teacher.

01:09.445 --> 01:11.822
I think I'm on his bad side.

01:13.282 --> 01:14.325
Why is that?

01:15.159 --> 01:18.954
Well, ever since that misunderstanding
about me filming him,

01:19.038 --> 01:20.039
he's been on my case.

01:20.706 --> 01:22.500
Nah. That can't be true.

01:23.459 --> 01:24.668
Yes, it's true.

01:24.752 --> 01:27.588
First, he embarrassed me by asking me
what my math grade was,

01:27.671 --> 01:29.799
and then he made me write
a reflection letter

01:29.882 --> 01:31.634
for simply not liking math.

01:31.717 --> 01:34.011
Now he's giving me demerits for no reason.

01:34.094 --> 01:35.471
[sighs]

01:35.554 --> 01:37.723
But he wouldn't do
something like that without reason.

01:40.518 --> 01:41.977
[owl hooting]

01:44.063 --> 01:45.064
Goodbye, Mr. Yoon.

01:45.147 --> 01:47.358
[chuckles] Yeah. See you tomorrow.

01:47.441 --> 01:49.235
-[Eui-ju] See you.
-[chuckles]

01:52.404 --> 01:53.864
[tense Western music playing]

01:53.948 --> 01:55.199
[Woo-su] Hey, Yoon!

01:55.282 --> 01:57.451
You ready to take
the Discrete Math lecture?

01:58.911 --> 02:00.496
[Eui-ju] No, no.

02:02.039 --> 02:03.749
[groans, sucks teeth]

02:03.833 --> 02:06.085
-The ending is a bit too flat.
-[whimsical music playing]

02:06.168 --> 02:10.130
Tae-ha shouldn't let Si-on
go on like this here.

02:10.214 --> 02:11.215
Math…

02:12.049 --> 02:14.552
[clicks tongue] I mean, Ju Si-on.

02:15.386 --> 02:17.513
I'm afraid you'll have to take a beating.

02:17.596 --> 02:19.598
[chuckles] It's going to hurt a little.

02:19.682 --> 02:22.768
You can blame your original's
real-life personality.

02:23.978 --> 02:25.521
-[sighs, clears throat]
-[knuckles crack]

02:26.689 --> 02:27.690
All right.

02:29.859 --> 02:31.443
HIS EYES BLAZE WITH OBSESSION…

02:31.527 --> 02:33.153
[dramatic, tense music playing]

02:33.779 --> 02:34.864
[Gi-jeon] Hey, Ju Si-on!

02:36.490 --> 02:38.200
-[grunts]
-[yelps, groans]

02:39.952 --> 02:41.120
TAE-HA PUNCHES SI-ON

02:41.203 --> 02:43.122
[panting]

02:50.713 --> 02:52.298
-Let's go.
-You're bleeding.

02:52.381 --> 02:54.216
-[Woo-su] I'm fine.
-[Eui-ju] No, wait, wait.

02:54.300 --> 02:56.552
One isn't enough. One more punch.

02:56.635 --> 02:58.012
Huh?

02:58.846 --> 03:00.222
[snickers]

03:00.306 --> 03:01.807
-One more punch?
-One more…

03:02.474 --> 03:04.310
Wait. Hold on.
Give me some time to brace myself.

03:04.393 --> 03:05.644
[groaning] Wait.

03:11.901 --> 03:13.152
[Eui-ju] There we go.

03:13.235 --> 03:14.737
That'll spice things up.

03:15.404 --> 03:17.281
[scoffs, clicks tongue]
Now it's much better.

03:17.364 --> 03:19.700
-[comical music playing]
-[chuckles]

03:21.076 --> 03:22.077
[sighs]

03:23.037 --> 03:24.121
This is so much fun.

03:24.204 --> 03:28.375
Man, it's a crime to keep this
only to myself? [groans]

03:29.168 --> 03:30.336
[sucks teeth]

03:30.419 --> 03:32.296
[sighs] Should I just post it?

03:35.299 --> 03:37.009
[gasps] I know, right?

03:37.968 --> 03:41.221
You guys want to go out
into the real world, right?

03:42.640 --> 03:44.725
If I am this desperate,

03:44.808 --> 03:47.561
to has to be much, much worse for you.

03:49.188 --> 03:52.566
[characters chanting] Do it! Do it! Do it!

03:56.111 --> 03:57.529
[Eui-ju] Should I just post it?

03:57.613 --> 03:59.657
-[no audible dialogue]
-[sighs]

04:00.157 --> 04:01.450
[chuckles]

04:11.293 --> 04:12.878
No one will notice it.

04:23.472 --> 04:24.598
SUBMIT A NEW PROJECT

04:27.601 --> 04:29.687
-[clicks on mouse]
-[children cheering]

04:29.770 --> 04:32.773
It's going out into the real world!

04:32.856 --> 04:34.316
WE WERE FRIENDS

04:34.400 --> 04:37.778
[fanfare music playing]

04:37.861 --> 04:39.196
[sighs] Good.

04:41.907 --> 04:45.619
CHAPTER 13: ARE HIS GLASSES
REALLY THAT BIG A DEAL?

04:51.458 --> 04:54.044
EPISODE 4

04:55.629 --> 04:56.714
Is it bad?

04:59.633 --> 05:00.634
Might get better.

05:01.218 --> 05:03.470
Who took them?
Not like anyone else could wear them.

05:05.305 --> 05:06.390
That's it!

05:08.392 --> 05:09.476
On the tree.

05:09.560 --> 05:11.061
You said you threw the glasses.

05:11.145 --> 05:13.605
If they're not on the ground,
they should be hanging on the tree.

05:14.189 --> 05:16.191
I thought the same
and checked the tree going home.

05:16.275 --> 05:17.276
But they weren't there.

05:18.694 --> 05:19.945
Then where could they be?

05:20.863 --> 05:22.865
Did a pigeon take them to build a nest?

05:24.074 --> 05:25.159
That's it!

05:25.242 --> 05:27.911
I hear birds like crows
have a thing for shiny objects.

05:27.995 --> 05:30.956
They steal things like that
to decorate their nests.

05:32.916 --> 05:34.251
Just get a new pair.

05:34.334 --> 05:37.755
The problem is it's not easy to order
those kinds of prescription glasses.

05:40.132 --> 05:41.300
Are you done?

05:42.760 --> 05:43.844
He can't even eat.

05:45.304 --> 05:46.388
A nest.

05:47.389 --> 05:48.390
[sighs]

05:52.978 --> 05:53.979
[sighs]

05:56.482 --> 05:57.733
[sighs]

06:02.571 --> 06:05.532
[moody music playing]

06:08.786 --> 06:09.787
[sighs]

06:16.710 --> 06:18.045
[toilet flushing]

06:19.046 --> 06:20.047
What's wrong with him?

06:22.216 --> 06:24.843
[clicks tongue] Goodness.
He's not feeling well.

06:24.927 --> 06:26.762
[coughing]

06:28.931 --> 06:30.641
I think I have to take a sick day.

06:31.141 --> 06:33.310
Okay, I will let the school know.

06:34.186 --> 06:36.522
-Get some rest today.
-[sighs]

06:36.605 --> 06:38.941
Geez, that pair of glasses is killing him.

06:41.276 --> 06:43.487
[Woo-su grunts, breathes heavily]

06:59.962 --> 07:01.630
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

07:01.713 --> 07:03.465
[chattering]

07:10.556 --> 07:11.807
[door closes]

07:12.391 --> 07:13.433
[chattering stops]

07:17.229 --> 07:19.356
Well, your homeroom teacher
isn't well today,

07:19.439 --> 07:21.859
so I'm here for your morning assembly
on his behalf.

07:21.942 --> 07:23.026
I'll take attendance.

07:24.027 --> 07:25.404
-Kim Ga-yeong.
-Here!

07:26.488 --> 07:27.489
Kim Dan-ji.

07:28.365 --> 07:30.242
-Here!
-Kim Yeong-jae.

07:30.325 --> 07:31.410
Here.

07:31.493 --> 07:32.995
-Oh A-rin.
-Here.

07:33.078 --> 07:35.205
-I wish we could change teachers.
-Choi Yu-mi.

07:35.289 --> 07:37.583
If Dong-ju was our homeroom teacher,
it'd be awesome.

07:38.083 --> 07:39.084
Yeah.

07:39.168 --> 07:40.586
-Jeon Ji-min.
-Here.

07:42.921 --> 07:45.257
Didn't Mr. Ga look fine until yesterday?

07:46.550 --> 07:49.052
Maybe he faked it
and went to meet his girlfriend.

07:49.136 --> 07:51.346
-Oh, man, that's crazy.
-[chuckles]

07:51.430 --> 07:54.975
Nah, I bet he's paying the price
for picking on Eui-ju, that's all.

07:55.058 --> 07:57.102
He shouldn't have given my boo a demerit.

07:57.186 --> 07:59.396
-Don't you agree? You're cute.
-Mmm.

07:59.479 --> 08:01.231
[giggles] Yeah.

08:03.609 --> 08:05.819
-Jenny, are you not on a diet?
-Hmm?

08:05.903 --> 08:07.196
-Why do you ask?
-Like that.

08:07.279 --> 08:08.697
-Like that.
-Wait. [chuckles]

08:08.780 --> 08:10.824
Hello, Mr. Ga. Are you feeling okay?

08:13.285 --> 08:15.829
Oh, no! I hope you get better soon.

08:15.913 --> 08:18.373
-[mysterious music playing]
-Don't worry about our class.

08:19.875 --> 08:22.586
Okay. I'll relay your message
during the dismissal.

08:23.712 --> 08:26.173
Yes, sure. Take care now. Bye.

08:27.257 --> 08:28.300
[giggles]

08:42.564 --> 08:45.025
I explained the concept
of Rolle's Theorem, right?

08:45.108 --> 08:48.195
So now, if you plug in one here…

08:49.404 --> 08:50.405
One…

08:50.989 --> 08:53.659
And then plug in five over here…

08:53.742 --> 08:54.743
[PA chiming]

08:56.745 --> 08:58.080
[teacher] That's it for today.

08:58.163 --> 08:59.873
[students] Thank you.

08:59.957 --> 09:02.251
[students cheer, laugh]

09:03.418 --> 09:04.878
[sighs] Finally.

09:05.587 --> 09:07.089
Attention, girls!

09:07.172 --> 09:09.341
Hey, is Mr. Ga coming to school tomorrow?

09:11.051 --> 09:13.595
After-school program applications
are due tomorrow.

09:13.679 --> 09:16.223
Don't forget to hand them in. That's all.

09:16.974 --> 09:18.767
Let's go to the cafeteria.

09:18.850 --> 09:21.645
-[stammers] Did she just ignore me?
-Mm-hmm.

09:21.728 --> 09:22.938
I have an art lesson.

09:23.522 --> 09:24.648
Bye.

09:25.941 --> 09:26.942
[students chattering]

09:29.653 --> 09:31.321
Is he sick for real?

09:33.740 --> 09:35.284
It's none of my business.

09:36.410 --> 09:37.411
[sniffs]

09:39.997 --> 09:40.998
MISSING GLASSES

09:41.081 --> 09:42.082
[Dong-ju sighs]

09:42.958 --> 09:45.460
[Gi-jeon] Woo-su might need time off
if he doesn't get better.

09:45.961 --> 09:48.088
-[Dong-ju sighs]
-[Gi-jeon] What did the doctor say?

09:48.171 --> 09:50.048
He needs absolute rest.

09:50.132 --> 09:53.135
If he pushes himself,
his other eye will be at risk.

09:53.218 --> 09:54.594
Oh, hi.

09:55.178 --> 09:56.471
That must be your application.

09:57.597 --> 10:00.309
And Mr. Ga's eyes… I mean, his glasses?

10:00.392 --> 10:02.894
Oh… that.

10:05.230 --> 10:07.232
[rueful music playing]

10:07.316 --> 10:10.736
Are those glasses that important to him?

10:14.364 --> 10:16.199
[Dong-ju]
Those glasses have a rare prescription.

10:16.283 --> 10:17.326
[panting]

10:17.409 --> 10:19.453
[Dong-ju] He was barely holding up,
but then he…

10:20.746 --> 10:24.249
We're concerned because it's going to take
a long time for him to get a new pair.

10:25.000 --> 10:26.668
[panting]

10:34.926 --> 10:36.803
Oh! Oh, no!

10:41.516 --> 10:42.601
Sir!

10:43.185 --> 10:45.520
-Hi. Aren't you going home?
-Oh, Ga-yun! Ga-yun, Ga-yun.

10:45.604 --> 10:47.356
-Stop, stop, stop!
-What? What is it?

10:47.439 --> 10:49.024
Let me… Let me borrow your bike.

10:49.107 --> 10:50.192
-I'll give it back later.
-My bike?

10:50.275 --> 10:51.276
I have to run after that truck.

10:51.360 --> 10:52.861
-Okay, okay. Wait, wait.
-Please let me use it.

10:52.944 --> 10:55.364
Thank you. [panting]

10:57.074 --> 10:59.034
[rock music playing]

10:59.117 --> 11:00.619
Out of the way!

11:00.702 --> 11:02.704
Sir! Wait, sir!

11:04.456 --> 11:05.457
[shouts]

11:12.798 --> 11:15.884
[groaning, panting]

11:17.761 --> 11:19.304
Sir!

11:20.055 --> 11:21.264
Sir!

11:22.724 --> 11:23.975
[groans] Come on!

11:26.228 --> 11:29.689
[groaning, panting]

11:32.526 --> 11:34.277
Sir! Sir, don't go!

11:34.361 --> 11:36.279
Hey! Sir! Sir!

11:36.363 --> 11:37.948
Please stop!

11:38.031 --> 11:39.533
[panting]

11:41.993 --> 11:42.994
[groaning]

11:43.578 --> 11:44.830
Stop!

11:44.913 --> 11:46.373
Please, sir! Stop!

11:50.127 --> 11:51.461
[shouts]

11:51.545 --> 11:53.088
Stop! Hey!

11:56.800 --> 11:58.051
Hey, please stop!

12:01.012 --> 12:03.223
[screaming]

12:06.476 --> 12:08.478
[panting] Sir!

12:08.562 --> 12:10.522
[wailing]

12:11.982 --> 12:13.775
Wait, mister!

12:13.859 --> 12:17.362
[yelling] When are you going to stop
and throw out the garbage?

12:18.864 --> 12:20.198
Sir, please stop!

12:21.992 --> 12:22.993
[groaning]

12:23.076 --> 12:24.995
Please stop, sir, stop!

12:25.495 --> 12:26.705
[panting]

12:28.540 --> 12:30.292
[shouting]

12:30.375 --> 12:32.210
[truck brakes squeal]

12:35.714 --> 12:38.091
What do you think you're doing?
That's dangerous!

12:38.175 --> 12:40.719
[sobbing] I'm sorry, sir. I'm sorry.
But I…

12:40.802 --> 12:43.054
Um, I need your help. Please, this once.

12:43.138 --> 12:45.932
My teacher's going to die without those…
[sobbing]

12:46.016 --> 12:47.601
What are you talking about, huh?

12:47.684 --> 12:50.562
So what happened is that I, um…

12:50.645 --> 12:52.814
I threw my teacher's glasses away

12:52.898 --> 12:56.485
and it turns out
he's going to die without those.

12:56.568 --> 12:58.403
[sad music playing]

12:58.487 --> 13:00.238
Please help me this once.

13:00.322 --> 13:03.325
Goodness, please let me check
if they're in there, sir.

13:03.408 --> 13:06.536
[sobbing] Please, sir.

13:06.620 --> 13:08.955
[plastic rustling]

13:09.039 --> 13:11.917
MUNICIPAL DUMP

13:12.000 --> 13:13.543
Are you sure they're in here?

13:13.627 --> 13:16.713
Yes, I threw them out
at the garbage dump yesterday.

13:18.006 --> 13:19.883
Why did you throw out
your teacher's glasses?

13:20.550 --> 13:22.093
[sobs] Beats me.

13:22.594 --> 13:24.471
If you tossed 'em,
why are you looking for 'em?

13:24.554 --> 13:26.056
[sighs] You're right.

13:26.640 --> 13:27.849
[groans]

13:27.933 --> 13:30.685
Sir, I'm so sorry. I'll find them quickly.

13:37.567 --> 13:40.403
[stammering] Um, sir. Thank you so much.

13:40.487 --> 13:41.571
I'll do it all myself.

13:41.655 --> 13:43.740
It's okay, I'll find them
and clean up quickly.

13:50.038 --> 13:51.039
Huh?

13:52.832 --> 13:54.167
[gasps] Oh! Hey, hey, hey!

13:55.669 --> 14:00.090
-[triumphant music playing]
-[shouts] Sir!

14:00.173 --> 14:01.466
Sir, I found them!

14:01.550 --> 14:02.551
You found them?

14:02.634 --> 14:05.011
[sobbing] Yes! These are his glasses.

14:06.596 --> 14:07.847
[driver groans]

14:07.931 --> 14:09.849
[sobbing]

14:11.351 --> 14:13.353
-Oh, thank you so much.
-Now, get going.

14:13.436 --> 14:14.437
Thank you so much.

14:14.521 --> 14:16.398
CHAPTER 14:
YOU BREAKING MY GLASSES

14:16.481 --> 14:18.608
CAUSED TEN MILLION WON'S
WORTH OF DAMAGE

14:22.612 --> 14:23.613
[sighs]

14:24.447 --> 14:25.657
Where did you find these?

14:27.450 --> 14:29.160
I found them on the poo-stained bench.

14:29.244 --> 14:30.829
Also, they were already broken.

14:33.665 --> 14:34.666
[sighs]

14:35.959 --> 14:37.002
4073.

14:41.047 --> 14:43.091
Those are the last four digits
of your phone number.

14:46.011 --> 14:49.264
One of my students has
the same last digits on her phone number.

14:49.347 --> 14:51.433
[dramatic music playing]

14:54.311 --> 14:56.104
YEO EUI-JU

14:56.187 --> 14:57.564
What's your name?

14:57.647 --> 14:59.566
[amusing music playing]

15:00.108 --> 15:01.651
It's none of your business.

15:01.735 --> 15:04.696
Just hurry up and pay me.
I gotta go to an Internet cafe.

15:04.779 --> 15:07.407
-Your name.
-It's Yeo Eui-do.

15:10.118 --> 15:11.119
[sighs]

15:11.620 --> 15:12.621
Call your sister.

15:13.371 --> 15:14.372
[groans] Why?

15:15.373 --> 15:18.084
-Do it.
-[groans, clicks tongue]

15:22.213 --> 15:23.506
[line ringing]

15:28.803 --> 15:31.056
[Eui-ju] Hey, what's up?

15:31.139 --> 15:32.974
Uh, I'll put him on the phone.

15:38.313 --> 15:39.314
Yeo Eui-ju.

15:48.990 --> 15:50.659
You stole your teacher's glasses?

15:50.742 --> 15:51.785
[chuckles] You're nuts.

15:53.578 --> 15:55.121
Now that she's here, you can leave.

15:56.247 --> 15:57.957
And watch how you speak to your sister.

16:07.926 --> 16:10.970
[stammers] Mr. Ga. [sniffles]

16:11.054 --> 16:13.723
[stammers] I can explain what happened.

16:13.807 --> 16:17.018
Didn't I ask you
if you had stepped on my glasses?

16:18.478 --> 16:22.232
You had a chance to come clean when
we were looking for them all together.

16:24.651 --> 16:27.362
I asked you at the parking lot
and you flat-out lied to me.

16:28.780 --> 16:30.699
I… [breathes shakily]

16:30.782 --> 16:31.783
I thought…

16:32.701 --> 16:35.870
you'd tell me off for
breaking your glasses if I told you.

16:36.621 --> 16:38.998
[sobs] But then… [sniffles]

16:39.082 --> 16:41.626
…you gave me as many as
four demerit points over Ji-a

16:41.710 --> 16:44.587
when I didn't do anything wrong at all.
[sniffles]

16:44.671 --> 16:46.464
I thought you were being too harsh on me.

16:47.048 --> 16:50.009
You were constantly on my case, so…

16:52.137 --> 16:55.223
[sniffles] This is all my fault. [sobbing]

16:55.306 --> 16:56.683
[tender music playing]

16:56.766 --> 16:59.519
I didn't know those glasses
were that important to you.

16:59.602 --> 17:01.479
Had I known how bad your vision was,

17:01.563 --> 17:03.648
I would've returned them to you
right away.

17:04.858 --> 17:07.068
[whimpering] I shouldn't have done it.

17:07.152 --> 17:09.821
[sniffles] I'm truly sorry about it.

17:11.990 --> 17:12.991
[sniffles]

17:19.038 --> 17:21.374
[sniffling]

17:24.294 --> 17:25.295
[sighs]

17:32.719 --> 17:33.720
[sighs]

17:34.721 --> 17:38.808
Well, it's clear who's in the wrong,
and you admitted it.

17:39.434 --> 17:40.685
So I need to be compensated.

17:41.728 --> 17:42.729
Compensated?

17:44.022 --> 17:47.150
When my glasses broke,
$6,000 went down the drain.

17:47.650 --> 17:52.071
$6,000? What kind of glasses
are worth that much? [sighs]

17:52.155 --> 17:53.823
It's not like I can take money
from a student,

17:53.907 --> 17:56.659
so you'll have to compensate me
with something other than money.

17:57.327 --> 18:00.330
Yes. Of course I'll compensate you.

18:00.830 --> 18:02.582
But how? With what?

18:03.374 --> 18:04.834
I'll give you one chance, okay?

18:06.044 --> 18:08.463
[gasps] Thank you, sir.

18:08.546 --> 18:10.006
I'll do anything you say.

18:10.882 --> 18:12.133
After-school math.

18:13.426 --> 18:15.345
-Excuse me?
-I'll give you a chance

18:15.428 --> 18:18.640
to find some passion for math
to help you improve your grade.

18:18.723 --> 18:19.724
[comical music playing]

18:19.808 --> 18:22.268
[chuckles] Uh, well, that's unnecessary.

18:22.769 --> 18:26.147
Uh, Mr. Ga, that program is for
top students, you know.

18:26.231 --> 18:27.941
Those who are first or second
in their classes.

18:28.024 --> 18:32.904
Hmm. Before class, set the classroom
temperature to 73 degrees Fahrenheit,

18:32.987 --> 18:36.699
place handouts on each desk, and collect
everyone's homework if there's any.

18:36.783 --> 18:38.952
Then after class,
clean up and lock the classroom.

18:39.577 --> 18:41.704
Oh, I can't do it. [sniffles]

18:44.624 --> 18:45.667
Every Wednesday.

18:46.459 --> 18:47.627
Every Wednesday?

18:48.753 --> 18:52.173
Mr. Ga, b-but I have after school PE
on Wednesdays.

18:52.257 --> 18:54.092
I really can't make it, Mr. Ga.

18:58.471 --> 18:59.472
Don't forget.

19:02.141 --> 19:03.268
Six thousand.

19:10.859 --> 19:12.026
[Eui-ju groans]

19:12.777 --> 19:16.072
[sighs] I really can't do it.

19:18.116 --> 19:19.492
[sobs] What do I do?

19:22.078 --> 19:23.079
[sighs]

19:24.581 --> 19:26.374
[sniffles, sighs]

19:27.500 --> 19:29.335
[sighs, groans]

19:35.216 --> 19:37.176
[groans] What is it this time?

19:37.260 --> 19:40.138
The reward.
I didn't get it because of you.

19:40.221 --> 19:41.556
Hey!

19:41.639 --> 19:44.809
I'm broke. I already spent
all my allowance for this month.

19:46.728 --> 19:48.229
-Mom!
-No! [stammers]

19:49.188 --> 19:50.231
Okay, fine.

19:56.571 --> 19:58.031
Here. That's all I have.

19:59.532 --> 20:01.075
Don't waste your allowance.

20:08.166 --> 20:12.837
[groaning] Why did I have to let him
get something on me?

20:12.921 --> 20:14.005
[cries]

20:14.589 --> 20:16.591
This is so darn annoying!

20:20.762 --> 20:22.263
[gasps] Hold on.

20:22.347 --> 20:24.557
It's clear who's in the wrong,
and you admitted it.

20:25.058 --> 20:26.476
So I need to be compensated.

20:27.060 --> 20:28.895
Don't forget. Six thousand.

20:29.771 --> 20:32.523
Math is actually quite good
with all his lines.

20:37.612 --> 20:38.613
[grunts]

20:43.201 --> 20:45.328
I bet it's somewhere at the bottom again.

20:45.411 --> 20:47.580
[inhales deeply, sighs]

20:48.748 --> 20:49.749
1. WE WERE FRIENDS

20:52.126 --> 20:53.127
Huh?

20:53.211 --> 20:55.672
WEB NOVEL RANKING
1. WE WERE FRIENDS

20:55.755 --> 20:58.257
-What? [stammers] First place?
-[triumphant music playing]

20:59.050 --> 21:00.259
Hold on… Hold on now.

21:00.343 --> 21:03.096
1. WE WERE FRIENDS
VIEWS: 130K

21:03.179 --> 21:04.389
Huh?

21:05.848 --> 21:07.600
WE WERE FRIENDS

21:08.184 --> 21:09.185
W-What's this?

21:09.978 --> 21:11.145
My followers are…

21:12.480 --> 21:13.982
One, two,

21:14.732 --> 21:16.401
three, four…

21:16.484 --> 21:17.527
FAVORITES 15,320

21:17.610 --> 21:22.156
15,320? [gasps, stammers] What the heck?

21:23.241 --> 21:25.660
What is this? What is going on?
Is it really mine?

21:27.954 --> 21:29.038
WE WERE FRIENDS - EPISODE 1

21:33.084 --> 21:36.421
[reader 1] I am from the future.
This novel will be a masterpiece soon.

21:36.504 --> 21:38.256
[reader 2] Let Yoon and Si-on
end up together please.

21:38.339 --> 21:41.426
[reader 3] Tae-ha's in true love.
I can't wait to read how it turns out

21:41.509 --> 21:43.261
-between Tae-ha and Yoon.
-What the heck? [gasps]

21:44.053 --> 21:46.889
[whimpers] Darn it. That hurts.

21:49.434 --> 21:52.061
It's not a dream?

21:52.145 --> 21:53.271
It's happening?

21:53.354 --> 21:55.231
[gasping]

21:57.358 --> 22:00.570
[reader 4] It's only the first episode,
but the air is darn tight already.

22:00.653 --> 22:02.655
[reader 5] My heart broke when he waited
with a sweet red bean bread.

22:02.739 --> 22:04.282
[reader 6]
What's more complex than Math is Yoon.

22:04.365 --> 22:05.491
[sighs] This line alone tells

22:05.575 --> 22:06.993
-the outlook of this story
-[giggles, squeals]

22:07.076 --> 22:09.328
[rock music playing]

22:10.079 --> 22:11.080
[chuckles]

22:11.164 --> 22:12.832
WE WERE FRIENDS - EPISODE 2

22:16.753 --> 22:18.129
WHAT? AM I TOO CLOSE?
YOON SHOOK…

22:24.218 --> 22:26.095
[Yeong-jae] Dan-ji found
Mr. Noh's Instagram.

22:26.179 --> 22:28.181
[Dan-ji]
I found a picture of him in college.

22:28.264 --> 22:30.767
[Go-ya] That's insane!
Find Dong-ju's Instagram too.

22:30.850 --> 22:32.643
[Dan-ji] How much do you offer?

22:32.727 --> 22:33.936
[Go-ya] Piss off.

22:34.020 --> 22:36.105
[Yeong-jae] What the--
Why is Eui-ju so quiet though?

22:36.189 --> 22:38.066
She can't be studying, can she?

22:39.192 --> 22:42.779
YOON SHOOK HIS HEAD BUT…

22:54.832 --> 22:56.084
You're late.

22:57.668 --> 22:58.753
I'm tired.

23:00.213 --> 23:01.756
We need to talk.

23:01.839 --> 23:02.840
I have nothing to say.

23:02.924 --> 23:05.051
When I ask for a talk,
you talk to me, got it?

23:05.134 --> 23:06.677
-I have nothing to say--
-Shut it!

23:06.761 --> 23:08.137
-Get off me!
-[grunts]

23:10.848 --> 23:11.849
[groans]

23:12.517 --> 23:14.519
-[scoffs]
-Sorry.

23:14.602 --> 23:15.770
[tense Western music playing]

23:15.853 --> 23:17.480
You should've let me go
when I told you to.

23:17.563 --> 23:19.482
-Are you okay? Let me see.
-[grunts]

23:20.942 --> 23:23.444
Well, it's clear who's in the wrong,
and you admitted it.

23:25.029 --> 23:26.614
So I need to be compensated.

23:28.366 --> 23:29.367
Compensated?

23:31.661 --> 23:32.662
[spits]

23:34.455 --> 23:35.456
Six thousand.

23:37.333 --> 23:38.501
What?

23:38.584 --> 23:41.254
I got a split lip,
that's 6,000 in damages.

23:41.838 --> 23:43.506
What are you talking about? Six thousand?

23:43.589 --> 23:45.424
That's the thing about rarity.

23:45.508 --> 23:49.929
The harder something is to get,
the more you want it to be yours.

23:51.097 --> 23:53.307
Same goes for my lips,
they aren't for just anyone.

23:54.142 --> 23:55.143
[chuckles]

23:56.853 --> 23:59.856
Since you're poor, you'll have to
compensate me with something else.

24:03.818 --> 24:05.236
Wednesday at 5:00 p.m.

24:05.903 --> 24:06.904
At my house.

24:08.281 --> 24:09.740
Don't be late.

24:13.870 --> 24:16.581
[scoffs] Six thousand.

24:21.627 --> 24:23.254
Let's see you make it up to me.

24:24.005 --> 24:26.007
[K-pop ballad playing]

24:48.237 --> 24:50.698
[Dong-ju] You're not intentionally
being harsh on Eui-ju, are you?

24:50.781 --> 24:52.783
Why are you so strict only with her?

24:52.867 --> 24:55.995
If your math teacher is blackmailing you
then blink your eyes twice.

24:56.579 --> 24:59.790
[Woo-su] I can't tolerate the fact that
Yeo Eui-ju has a four in math.

24:59.874 --> 25:03.294
You keep pushing me to have dark ideas.
Yeo Eui-ju.

25:03.377 --> 25:06.297
I didn't know you were this hopeless.
I'm disappointed in you.

25:06.380 --> 25:08.549
Did Kang Tae-ha say
he'd wait for you at your house again?

25:08.633 --> 25:10.760
-[Dong-ju] I don't know. Don't touch me.
-[chuckles]

25:10.843 --> 25:12.678
Hey, what's so funny, huh?

25:13.179 --> 25:14.805
-Is it rated-R or BL?
-[sighs]

25:14.889 --> 25:17.391
This is it. This is the one.

25:17.475 --> 25:20.353
This is a perfect ending that calls for
the next episode!
